Project: Autokit
Goal: AI-powered lightweight drum sampler plugin for Linux (Arch + Hyprland)
Features:
  - Auto-generate drum kits from user samples
  - Randomization with lockable pads/lanes
  - 16-step sequencer with pattern variation
  - Dark neon-themed GTK3 UI (Wayland-ready)
  - Runs as LV2 (primary) and optionally VST3
  - Secure, sandboxed, open-source

Phases:
  1: ProjectSetup
    - Create GitHub repo (MIT or GPLv3)
    - Define modular architecture (core engine, UI, plugin wrappers)
    - Setup CMake build system and CI pipeline
  2: CoreAudioEngine
    - Sample playback and pad/kit structure
    - Step sequencer (16-32 steps, swing, velocity, polyrhythms)
    - MIDI in/out support
    - Expose plugin parameters (volume, pitch, etc.)
  3: AI_ML_SampleAnalysis
    - Scan sample folders, extract audio features (Essentia/librosa)
    - Cluster samples into 2D map (t-SNE/UMAP)
    - Classify samples (kick/snare/hat/etc.)
    - Pattern generator (random + Markov/heuristic)
  4: GTK3_UI
    - Dark neon-themed UI with:
      * Sample map (zoom/pan, hover preview)
      * 16-pad grid (lockable, color-coded)
      * Step sequencer (click/drag, velocity, rolls)
      * Randomize, lock, undo/redo buttons
      * Theme customization (CSS-based)
  5: PluginIntegration
    - LV2 wrapper (control ports, Atom messaging, GTK UI)
    - Optional VST3 wrapper (JUCE/iPlug2 or direct SDK)
    - Ensure Renoise compatibility (LV2 focus)
  6: Testing_Optimization
    - Unit and integration tests (core + UI)
    - Performance profiling (CPU, memory, latency)
    - Host testing (Renoise, Carla, Bitwig, etc.)
    - Beta testing with Linux audio users
  7: Docs_Deployment
    - Write user manual and developer guide
    - Include demo kits/patterns (free samples)
    - Package LV2 plugin (AUR, GitHub Releases)
    - Launch GitHub repo and announce to community

SystemArchitecture:
  CoreAudioEngine:
    - Language: C++17/20
    - Features: low-latency, real-time safe, standalone library
    - DSP: sample playback, sequencing, effects
  PluginAPI:
    - LV2 primary target (using lilv/DPF)
    - Optional VST3 (JUCE/iPlug2 or direct SDK)
    - Shared core logic for both formats
  SampleAnalysis_AI:
    - Feature extraction (spectral centroid, MFCC, etc.)
    - Dimensionality reduction (t-SNE/UMAP)
    - Sample classification (kick, snare, hat, percussion)
    - Pattern generation (random, Markov chains, AI models)
  UI:
    - GTK3 with C++ wrapper (gtkmm or Glib/GTK)
    - Dark neon theme, customizable colors
    - Sample map visualization (OpenGL/Vulkan optional)
    - 16-pad grid with locks and color coding
    - Step sequencer with pattern editing and randomization
    - Undo/redo history for kit and pattern changes
    - File browser and sample database (SQLite or JSON)
    - Performance optimized for CPU/GPU, scaling support
  Security:
    - No network access, offline operation
    - Restricted file I/O to user sample dirs
    - Safe file parsing (libsndfile)
    - Optional sandbox mode, minimal logging

DevelopmentPlan:
  Step1: Requirements_Design
    - Finalize features and UI wireframes
    - Study Atlas 2 and XO workflows
    - Identify gaps and improvements (undo, Linux support, theming)
    - User feedback from target audience
  Step2: ProjectSetup_Architecture
    - GitHub repo with license
    - Repo structure: src/, plugins/, docs/, tests/, data/
    - CMake build and CI setup
    - Development guidelines and contribution docs
  Step3: CoreAudioEngine_Dev
    - Implement sampler voice and drum kit structure
    - Step sequencer synced to host tempo
    - MIDI input/output handling
    - Automatable parameters
    - Optional effects (bitcrusher, filter, compressor)
    - Unit tests for non-realtime parts
  Step4: SampleAnalysis_AI
    - Library scanning and feature extraction
    - Dimensionality reduction for sample map
    - Sample classification and filtering
    - Pattern generation with random and AI methods
    - Undo/redo history implementation
  Step5: GUI_Development
    - Main window layout with sample map and pads
    - Sample map rendering with zoom/pan and previews
    - Pad grid and step sequencer UI
    - Controls: volume, swing, tempo, randomize buttons
    - Theme customization and scaling
    - Wayland/Hyprland compatibility testing
  Step6: PluginWrappers
    - LV2 plugin bundle with GTK UI
    - MIDI and parameter port implementation
    - Optional VST3 wrapper (JUCE or direct SDK)
    - Testing in multiple hosts (Renoise, Carla, Bitwig)
  Step7: Testing_Optimization
    - Functional and performance testing
    - Memory usage optimization
    - Cross-environment and user beta testing
  Step8: Documentation_Demo
    - User manual and developer docs
    - Demo samples and preset patterns
    - Licensing and credits
  Step9: Deployment_Community
    - Release binaries and packaging (AUR, Flatpak)
    - Announcements on Linux audio forums
    - Open issue tracker and contribution encouragement
    - Ongoing maintenance and future milestones